  "implementation": [
    "Arc Deformable reuses the uniform Rebuild solve with endpoint tangent projection on a normalized unit arc. Full circles reuse the existing Circle layouts.",
    "Arc output conversion is shared by command execution, ordinary final-point previews, Tilted and Tangent previews. Native-smlib delegates only interpolation to the existing rebuild backend.",
    "Degree 2..11 and PointCount degree+2..1000 getters validate independently and in order. Retained low counts are accepted only when construction still has more controls than degree.",
    "Successful constructions persist Arc settings outside document history. Native next-getter receipts independently witness successful, exact and cancelled preference behavior.",
    "Deformable Midpoint numeric output starts at its input radial seam; exact Midpoint construction retains the symmetric sweep. The raw typed-endpoint timeout remains diagnostic.",
    "Center length input supports signed scalars, explicit clockwise direction and arbitrary spatial distance points while retaining the construction plane."
  ],
  "input_calibration": "Physical native click and hover receipts calibrate authored inputs using public viewport rays, including the initial cursor. Expected output geometry never supplies construction inputs.",
  "raw_capture_policy": [
    "Basic rows are original initial indices [0,2,4,6,8,9,10]. Ordered rows are boundaries indices [0,1,2,3,5,6,8,9,10,11].",
    "Constructions preserve modes indices [0,1,2,3,6..24]. Two earlier Midpoint captures timed out because the driver did not recognize the Midpoint prompt. The prompt prefix was corrected before new captures.",
    "Settings preserve preferences indices [0,1,2,4,5,6,7,8,9]. The excluded low-count Enter capture remains raw: Enter retains the invalid getter default and subsequent coordinates cannot finish construction.",
    "Raw boundary rows with point count <= degree report a native Arc Success event and no output. They are not relabeled as native failures.",
    "The six-row Midpoint diagnostic batch did not respond within 240 seconds. Two smaller captures preserve negative-angle and endpoint diagnostics, plus length/default retry input. A clean numeric subset qualifies unchanged.",
    "The original boundaries launch failed when the harness rejected an explicitly cancelled setup. The corrected bounded harness accepts clean, complete cancellation and a later launch produced the preserved raw response."
  ],
